Date/count arithmetic: in the relevant 7-day period, they called 10 times about one card. Regulation F’s threshold for covered debt collectors is more than 7 calls in 7 consecutive days; 10 − 7 = 3 calls over that federal threshold. But because the caller is the original bank collecting in its own name, that federal threshold does not by itself let you sue under the FDCPA/Regulation F.

